# T6b. The parser hangs `return: addN` on the model's own frame; `n: 5` follows it in the text.
# A statement after the return of a callable merge is refused, not run before the build.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + x
    return: addN
    n: 5

add5: makeAdder 5
int: a (add5: 1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: a; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
